{"meta":{"ticker":"IHE","as_of_date":"2026-05-22","performance_as_of":"2026-04-30","generated_at":"2026-05-23 08:39:33"},"benchmark":{"ticker":"SPY","fund_name":"State Street SPDR S&P 500 ETF"},"overview":{"ticker":"IHE","fund_name":"iShares U.S. Pharmaceuticals ETF","category":"US Health Care","issuer":"BlackRock","index_name":"DJ US Select / Pharmaceutical","region":"North America","exchange":"NYSEARCA","expense_ratio":0.0038,"aum":883622075,"holdings_count":59,"inception_date":"2006-05-01","overall_score":8.7783203125,"overall_rank":140,"sector_diversification_score":1},"description":{"tsi_description":"IHE is a concentrated pharmaceuticals ETF that tracks the Dow Jones U.S. Select Pharmaceuticals Index and provides targeted exposure to U.S. drug manufacturers and vaccine producers. The fund uses a float-adjusted market-cap-weighting approach, resulting in substantial allocations to a handful of large pharmaceutical companies. Unlike broader healthcare ETFs, IHE offers more direct exposure to pharmaceutical industry earnings cycles, product development trends, and merger activity. The portfolio combines higher-growth pharmaceutical companies with more mature and lower-valuation firms, resulting in a balanced mix of growth and defensive characteristics. Overall, IHE offers a tactical and industry-specific approach to pharmaceutical investing.","strategy_steps":["Tracks the Dow Jones U.S. Select Pharmaceuticals Index.","Invests in U.S. companies involved in pharmaceutical manufacturing, prescription drugs, over-the-counter drugs, and vaccine production.","Uses a float-adjusted market-capitalization weighting methodology.","Maintains concentrated exposure to the industry's largest pharmaceutical companies.","Includes approximately 55 holdings.","Allows larger pharmaceutical companies to receive heavier portfolio weights based on market capitalization.","Rebalances and reconstitutes quarterly.","Uses a passive indexing approach to replicate index performance."],"best